 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 542 people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $321K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Heritage Insurance Holdings, In is a small-cap financial services business with a $984M market cap on $847M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $174M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.93\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 34\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 55% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 84% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"HRTG Q3 Earnings Call Highlights Pricing Pressure and Growth Plans","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023374/hrtg-q3-earnings-call-highlights-pricing-pressure-and-growth-plans?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog_plus%7Cearnings_call_takeaways-3023374","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793813760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Heritage Insurance (HRTG) a Great Value Stock Right Now?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/heritage-insurance-hrtg-great-value-134002940.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793626802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.958,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Heritage Insurance (HRTG)